        "text": "$mR\\omega^2 = GMm / R^2$ and $\\omega = 2\\pi / T$ or $mv^2 / R = GMm / R^2$ and $v = 2\\pi R / T$ or $4\\pi^2mR / T^2 = GMm / R^2$"
      },
      {
        "mark": "A1",
        "text": "correct completion of algebra to get $T^2 = (4\\pi^2 / GM) R^3$, with identification of $(4\\pi^2 / GM)$ as $k$"
